1. Where the searched step of R+S clips at q = 32, on the 42 matrices of layers (0, 8, 16, 24, 32, 40)
   clip limit in standard deviations of the row: least 2.22, median 3.27, most 3.92
   share of entries clipped: 0.1842 %
   The clip probes use one limit, 3.45, on every matrix. So they touch nearly the entries R+S clips, not exactly those.

2. What XR at q = 32 clips when its step is multiplied by 0.7
   share of entries clipped: 0.8645 %
   largest entry of a row, in standard deviations of the row: median over rows 2.3 to 4.8 by matrix, 99th percentile 2.3 to 14.1
   so the limit, 0.7 of the row's largest entry, is 1.6 to 3.4 standard deviations for the median row and higher for rows with a large entry. No entry is cut by more than 30 percent.

